# hilavitkutin-build

Build-time optimisation crate. cfg emission, LLVM pass configuration,
PGO/BOLT workflows, pragma system. A crate takes it as a
build-dependency and writes one line, `hilavitkutin_build::script!(<prototype>)`,
in a build script it keeps wherever it wants. The first build writes
the rustc wrapper and its `.cargo/config.toml` line into the workspace
by itself, and the builds after it take the flags. The flags reach the
consumer's own workspace members only, never its dependencies. The
linker, the backend, LTO and the other build choices are pragmas too,
and one script of a workspace names the ones that reach all of it.
